# Round 18, C2-1 (fixed). L §5.10 The sign rule: checked "2. after each decision's legs, or the observations booked at its
# point, ... as they are booked"; E §4.2 step 5: "in step 3, each decision's legs together ...; in step 3, that
# decision's legs at the place". c is a claim (min 0) at 50.00 PLN; the decision d takes bal(c) + 50 = 100.00 PLN out of
# it and puts back 100.00 PLN, which leaves c at 50.00 PLN and konto at 100.00 PLN: no refusal (q; snap11 refused the
# first leg, as E's old "the leg just booked"). With back = 40.00 PLN the legs leave c at -10.00 PLN: refused, with d's
# legs at c, both (flows of each), and the balances they touch from there (q2; L §8.4 `<movement> takes <claim> below 0`).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place c: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
kind shifts: event certain
  leg out: PLN
  leg back_in: PLN
input extra: money PLN
input back: money PLN
input day: date

move d: shifts
  on day
  reads c
  leg out from c to konto amount bal(c) + extra
  leg back_in from world to c amount back

ask q: bal(c, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask q2: bal(c, 2026-03-31), flows(d.out, 2026-03), flows(d.back_in, 2026-03), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) with back = 40.00 PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  extra = 50.00 PLN
  back = 100.00 PLN
  day = 2026-03-10
  opening[c] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
q: (50.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
q2: (refused: RUN-PLACE d takes c below 0, refused: RUN-PLACE d takes c below 0, refused: RUN-PLACE d takes c below 0, refused: RUN-PLACE d takes c below 0)
  pinned: back = 40.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
